ing, l'objectif est donc vraiment de relâcher pour garder au maximum ton énergie pour les séances intenses !","test":false,"importance":false,"trainingType":"EF","trainingCategory":"road_basic_endurance","exercisesBlocks":[{"repeat":1,"exercises":[{"_t":"SmartExercise","name":"EF_45","exerciseType":"running","pace":{"name":"EF","value":327,"kind":"range","zoneKind":"Z2","abstract":false,"slug":"ef"},"durations":[{"value":45,"timeUnit":"minutes"}],"manualLap":false}]}],"difficulty":1,"trainingIndex":4,"weekDate":1788134400000,"status":"todo","stats":{"_t":"SessionExpectedStats","expectedDistance":7.894736842105263,"expectedDuration":2700},"paceZones":[{"kind":"Z2","duration":2700,"pace":{"value":327}}]},{"_t":"SmartSessionWithStats","sport":"road","name":"S60_600_3_Alternative1","description":"Séance de S60 (sans S60), en \"over/under\", où l'on va encadrer la vitesse cible. Elle est composée de **4 séries** de 5' avec 2' de repos entre chaque série. Chaque 5' est composée de **2' au S30 suivi par 3' au SweetSpot, enchainé sans repos**. ","displayName":"Séance S60 alternative : \"Big Five\"","coachAdvice":"Mettre des petites accélérations en course c'est la signature des coureurs Kenyans. Reproduire cette variation d'allure poncutellement à l'entrainement a pour avantage d'apprendre à maitriser différentes allures sans récupération et ainsi d'étendre notre zone de confort.","test":false,"importance":false,"trainingType":"Intensity","trainingCategory":"road_intensity","exercisesBlocks":[{"repeat":1,"exercises":[{"_t":"SmartExercise","name":"WU_15","exerciseType":"warm-up","pace":{"name":"EF","value":327,"kind":"range","zoneKind":"Z2","abstract":false,"slug":"ef"},"durations":[{"value":15,"timeUnit":"minutes"}],"manualLap":true}],"blockType":"warm-up"},{"repeat":4,"exercises":[{"_t":"SmartExercise","name":"S30_2","exerciseType":"running","pace":{"name":"Seuil 30","value":241,"kind":"single-value","zoneKind":"Z4","abstract":false,"slug":"seuil30"},"durations":[{"value":